# QEMU overrides on top of sdkconfig.defaults:
#   idf.py -DSDKCONFIG_DEFAULTS="sdkconfig.defaults;sdkconfig.defaults.qemu" build
#
# QEMU's esp32s3 machine does not answer IDF's PSRAM chip-ID probe
# (espressif/qemu#129), so PSRAM must stay off there; with the probe off IDF
# leaves 356 KiB of internal RAM rather than 133 KiB.  QEMU also emulates a
# 4 MB flash with the older layout, hence 4 MB here.
#
# esp-emu (Espressif's emulator) needs none of this: it models 8 MB PSRAM and
# reads the 16 MB flash size from the image header, so it uses the plain
# sdkconfig.defaults and passes --psram-size 8M (its default).
CONFIG_ESPTOOLPY_FLASHSIZE_4MB=y
# CONFIG_SPIRAM is not set
